  clock: 6  # d312
  nonce: d312  # d312
  message: "PROGRESS (Python EXTENDS half): external/stdlib base classes now emit an unresolved-external `extends` edge (from-imported bases like Enum/Protocol/ABC/App/Widget + bare builtins like Exception/str) instead of dropping the relationship — py.py `_extract_inheritance_edges`, mirroring the landed JS/TS A2 fallback. Confidence stays EVIDENCE-DERIVED (ast_extends->0.95, ADR-0039 — not the JS/TS-era 0.5 emitter constant; is_resolved=False carries the unresolved target). New `_base_module_is_in_tree` guard (suffix-tolerant vs module_to_file_id) drops a not-yet-extracted IN-TREE base rather than minting a workspace-prefixed phantom (INV-nuzas-safe); aliased in-tree bases re-resolve on the original name. Dogfood (linkers dir): previously-dropped ABC base now emits, 0 workspace-prefixed external extends. 9 new tests + 1 pre-existing updated; smart-test 3141 passed / 100% cov. REMAINING (item stays todo_hard): the INSTANTIATES half (2333 external constructors mistyped as calls), the Kotlin+Ruby analyzer analogues, and the framework-agnostic core inheritance-linker chokepoint (Approach C) which also handles dotted/qualified bases (argparse.X, deferred here)."  # d312
