  message: "PROGRESS (Python INSTANTIATES half): external constructor calls now type as `instantiates` (evidence ast_new, is_resolved=False) instead of misfiling as plain `calls`. PascalCase heuristic (Python's strong class-naming convention) at the two unresolved-external emit sites — bare `Path()`/`MagicMock()` (py.py:5158) and `module.ClassName()` e.g. argparse.ArgumentParser() (py.py:4727); snake_case callables (join, os.getcwd) stay `calls`. Full self-analysis: calls 65134->63220, instantiates 8394->10312 (~1918 external constructions recovered, was 0-external). Confidence 0.95 evidence-derived. Targets stay external/unresolved so in-repo reachability/dead-code unaffected; shifts edge_type counts + centrality weights -> awaits_bakeoff_validation. 4 new tests, smart-test 20673 passed / 100% cov. REMAINING (item stays todo_hard): Kotlin+Ruby extends/instantiates analogues + the framework-agnostic core inheritance-linker chokepoint (Approach C, also handles dotted/qualified extends bases like argparse.X). Non-PascalCase external constructors (rare) + other call forms (~415 of the est. 2333) also remain."  # 0ed3
