- op: discuss  # 8088
  at: '2026-07-13T23:45:29Z'  # 8088
  by: agent  # 8088
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8088
  clock: 9  # 8088
  nonce: '8088'  # 8088
  message: "Approach-C core-linker chokepoint DONE (PR 70d0cc067e, dev). The framework-agnostic inheritance-linker (hypergumbo_core/linkers/inheritance.py) no longer drops a base that resolves to no in-tree symbol — it mints an is_resolved=False external extends edge to an external_symbol boundary node ({lang}:external:0-0:{name}:unresolved, the INV-nuzas-safe 'external' sentinel, dst_ref=None), evidence-derived 0.95 (ADR-0039). Generalizes the external-base fallback (previously Python+JS/TS per-analyzer only) to EVERY OO language and recovers Python dotted bases (class C(argparse.X)) py.py defers. Ownership split prevents double-emission: a per-analyzer fallback owns a class's BARE external bases (resolves import aliases to the ORIGINAL name, invisible to the chokepoint), so when an analyzer already emitted an external edge for a class the chokepoint defers its bare bases and adds only the dotted ones + all bases for languages with no analyzer fallback (Kotlin/Ruby/etc). Self-contained in inheritance.py, 100% cov.\n\nEXTENDS external-drop bug (the 23.4%-base-less-classes headline) FULLY FIXED for all OO languages. Evidence — production-path full-pipeline tests: test_python_ast_analysis::test_run_extends_dotted_qualified_base_emitted_by_chokepoint, test_csharp::test_external_base_class_emits_unresolved_extends; 4-language dogfood (Kotlin UserController->AbstractController, Ruby User->ActiveRecord::Base, Python-dotted GroupedFmt->argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter recover, Python-bare Color->Enum stays py.py precise, 0 dup edges). Real case: cli.py:253 GroupedSubcommandHelpFormatter(argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter) was dropped, now emits.\n\nRESIDUALS (P1->P3, not closed — separate mechanisms, NOT the extends drop): (1) external INSTANTIATES for non-Python is GREENFIELD — Kotlin/Ruby emit NO instantiates edges (Ruby .new is a calls edge; Kotlin emits nothing), so no dropped constructor to recover — new constructor-detection feature work; Python instantiates external already fixed in the campaign. (2) Retiring the now-redundant per-analyzer _extract_inheritance_edges resolvers is a refactor. Both distinct from this item's drop bug."  # 8088
